.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_FREE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_free \- free a response and every resource that it owns
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

void chttpclient_resp_free(chttpcli_response *resp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function frees the buffer of the response body, the map of the
response headers, and the response struct itself. A call with NULL is
safe.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A response carries its own copy of the allocator procs of the client
that made it, and it does not refer to that client. You can therefore
free a response before or after chttpclient_destroy of the client. The
functions that a custom allocator names must still be callable.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_count (3),
